{%- comment -%}
  Besjaar 11.6.18 — footer assurance band.

  Was three chunky cards, each a third of a phone screen tall, icon stacked
  above centred text. Now one quiet band: three columns divided by hairlines,
  no card chrome, a small sky icon disc per item. Roughly a tenth of the
  height, and it reads as a reassurance line rather than a feature section.

  Phones: icon above a short label, centred, supporting line small beneath.
  From 700px: icon to the left of the text, left aligned, larger type.

  Selectors are deliberately specific — the earlier footer rules in the
  desktop carrier were being outranked here.
  2026-09-13 consolidation: this section's <style> block was extracted during
  the CSS bundling pass. The rules above are now served from
  assets/besjaar-seo-carriers-late.css, loaded by besjaar-desktop-fixes-1170.
  Editing this file changes nothing — edit the bundle instead. The section is
  kept so existing header-group settings stay valid.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Besjaar footer polish",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "11.6.18: the footer assurance block is one hairline-divided band of three columns instead of three stacked cards — compact on phones, icon-left rows from 700px. Keep in the header group after the desktop section."
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
